      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "The given numbers are $0$, $2z$, $4z$, $8z$, and $16z$.\n\nTo find the average value of these numbers, we need to sum them up and then divide the total sum by the number of elements.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Sum} = 0 + 2z + 4z + 8z + 16z\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the sum:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Sum} = 0 + 2z + 4z + 8z + 16z = 30z\n\\]\n\nNext, we divide the sum by the number of elements, which is 5:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average value} = \\frac{\\text{Sum}}{\\text{Number of elements}} = \\frac{30z}{5}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the fraction:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average value} = \\frac{30z}{5} = 6z\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the average value of the given numbers is \\(\\boxed{6z}\\).",
